ar.com", "published": "2026-09-15T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxOM2NHNy1zRy1tRkdHMFpWck80aHUtTGhjN0p5c2ZvNmp0NGhpcWxNWnZ2RFFpOFdtWFZzY1NSSjRmc0xBcmpPUkNPejM2N3hZZXdTc2JpWlM4b3RsQy1nVEEyYTVuSmhWSDc3dlRXMFJqYTVzZFlNR3VTUDVLTjIzaGgwOWF6dzVDX3B5QXRNdnpzb0I4QXc?oc=5"}, {"title": "Dunlap proposes four debates against LePage", "source": "mainemorningstar.com", "published": "2026-09-09T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxOSW4yNy02WTZ2RUdrYUV2eHdmVzktc3h4MW1acXllOVViamd0YUhTTEtBUUcxaUM0QzBudjRiTmkyRllEa185SHZiNlo2T2ItaXE3cnZMb1RxNFhrc09ualdTTGFiNUZpem1Ld29fV0VxSFRwQ0JDTXRtTnk5alJnMVJDQmZBcEp3cTZpVA?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": -0.7, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 3.07, "poll_sd": 6.5, "poll_weight": 0.38, "fundamentals": {"margin": 3.96, "lean": -4.0, "environment": 8.4, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -0.44}, "rating_margin": -3.8, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 6.27, "baseline_margin": 0.74, "analyst_adjustment": -2.24, "key_factors": ["Open seat in an R-leaning district (PVI R+4) with Golden not on the ballot", "Expert ratings tilt Republican: five call it Lean/Likely R, four Tossup", "LePage holds a large fundraising and cash-on-hand advantage", "Prediction markets price Dunlap around 33-35%"], "rationale": "The seat's Republican lean, the absence of incumbent Golden, LePage's money edge, and a rating consensus of Tilt R outweigh the recent UNH poll showing Dunlap up six, since most other surveys are even or Democratic-sponsored. Markets and raters both point modestly Republican, so a small Republican edge with wide uncertainty fits the evidence.", "watch": "The October debates and whether Dunlap can consolidate the district's Democratic base despite its Trump-era lean; a second strong independent poll could shift this back to Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Jared Golden (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Maine's 2nd District is an open seat this cycle, with Democrat Jared Golden retiring after several narrow wins in a district that leans Republican by about four points. State Auditor Matt Dunlap carries the Democratic banner against former two-term governor Paul LePage, a well-known and polarizing figure who has outraised Dunlap and holds a large cash advantage heading into the fall.\n\nRecent polling is mixed: a University of New Hampshire survey in late September showed Dunlap ahead by six, while earlier surveys were essentially even, and most of those came from Democratic sponsors. Expert raters split between Tossup and Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Dunlap roughly a one-in-three chance. The race sits on a knife's edge, with ranked-choice tabulation possibly decisive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4353, "margin": -1.5}]}